    <string name="msg_187" formatted="false">"Date / Version / Changes"</string>
    <string name="msg_188" formatted="false">"2026-10-16 · 1.4.1\nAdded an optional switch to start app battery monitoring with performance monitoring, off by default and applied on the next start. Stopping saves linked recordings while independent battery monitoring continues. Hide, pause and manual battery stops do not restart it. Missing Shizuku permission is reported.\n\n2026-10-16 · 1.4.0\nAdded automatic GitHub Releases update checks on opening the main screen, enabled by default. About offers manual checks and an automatic-check switch. New releases show their version, notes and APK download link. Numeric version comparison prevents downgrade prompts; network errors, rate limits and missing APKs are handled explicitly.\n\n2026-10-16 · 1.3.2\nThe whole drawer now slides in and out from the left with a fading scrim. Selecting a destination closes it before the page transition. First-time pages animate after layout; reused pages also transition. Rapid selection keeps the latest destination, and cancellation clears pending navigation.\n\n2026-10-16 · 1.3.1\nHold the time-step buttons to keep moving; release, move outside or reach an endpoint to stop. Murasame moves to the left and the title to the right. Tap the avatar to open a one-third-width drawer, fully hidden when closed. Its avatar covers the page avatar; tap it, the outside area or Back to close.\n\n2026-10-15 · 1.3.0\nAdded phone clock timestamps alongside elapsed time and configurable cursor steps on the chart page. Step limits appear only for invalid input. Added a collapsible left navigation rail that expands to one third of the available width, with inline time-range and deletion tools.\n\n2026-10-13 · 1.2.1\nSmoother card and page navigation with retained pages and scroll positions, brief transitions and touch feedback. Battery details use a separate view; Back returns to the list and selected chart intervals are preserved.\n\n2026-10-13 · 1.2.0\nAdded independent background app battery recording, consumption shares and mAh, time ranges and interval-average power charts. Foreground is opaque, background translucent, and unclassified consumption hatched.\n\n2026-10-10 · 1.1.0\nRedesigned bottom navigation, performance overview, overlay preview and graph cards. Added persistent Dark, Light and System themes.\n\n2026-10-10 · 1.0.0\nAdded Japanese, English, French and German, with system or manual language selection. Removed the home subtitle and icon creation note.\n\n2026-10-08 · 0.4.0\nAutomatic recording enabled by default. Monitoring starts recording; stopping saves it. All metrics are recorded independently of overlay selection. Added 15 stacked graphs with shared timeline, synchronized cursor, last/selected values and min/max/mean. Kept sample, range and session deletion.\n\n2026-10-07 · 0.3.0\nRenamed to MurasameRTSS with Murasame icon. Added manual recording, metric selection, time ranges and deletion of points, ranges or sessions. Added About and changelog.\n\n2026-10-07 · 0.2.1\nFixed unnecessary wrapping in landscape. Measure available width again on rotation.\n\n2026-10-07 · 0.2.0\nAdded Shizuku presentation FPS, frame time and device power estimate. Explained GPU access limits and improved diagnostics.\n\n2026-10-07 · 0.1.0\nInitial release: manual controls, persistent notification, top overlay, CPU group clocks, temperatures, memory and battery monitoring. Configurable metrics, font and background opacity with touch-through."</string>
